        "original_id": "aa719035-ddba-5858-bd39-418ac96e18ad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2, Douglas SBD Dauntless, Curtiss SB2C Helldiver\n- Organizations: United States Navy, Douglas Aircraft\n- Events: invasion of Lae-Salamaua\n- Places: Lae, New Guinea\n\nFacts:\n- From 1940 through 1944, Douglas Aircraft manufactured the Douglas SBD Dauntless.\n- The Douglas SBD Dauntless was a World War II American naval scout plane and dive bomber.\n- On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the United States Navy aircraft carriers USS Lexington and USS Yorktown damaged the Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2 off Lae, New Guinea.\n- The Curtiss SB2C Helldiver replaced the Douglas SBD Dauntless in United States Navy service.",
